summary:
  A tick of "This computer" changes the balance while a level still waits
  to be multiplied by it.

history:
  What a device is told waits 400 ms as a master. Unticked inside that
  window, a device due 0.100 was sent the old master times the new
  balance, 0.050; ticked the other way, 0.200. The tick sends what waits
  first.

target:
  package/contents/ui/main.qml

find:
          _castFlush();   // a level that still waits was asked for under the balance of before the tick

replace:
          // a level that still waits was asked for under the balance of before the tick

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_invariants.py::test_a_tick_on_this_computer_does_not_reinterpret_a_level_that_still_waits.
  The behaviour itself is tests/qml/tst_volumeroad.qml::test_a_tick_while_a_level_still_waits_sends_it_as_it_was_asked,
  on a copy of the tick. Line-neutral.
